## Module-by-Module Execution Strategy

### Phase 2: Fix All Errors & Compile
- Ensure frontend `oxlint` passes cleanly.
- Verify `cargo check` and `cargo build` run flawlessly on the backend.
- Catch any React hydration or console warnings across pages.

### Phase 3 & 4: Database & Removing Dummy Data
- **Target Files:** Remove static mock arrays and fake API responses across the frontend `services` and `pages`.
- **MongoDB Integration:**
  - Route all frontend pages through the Axum REST endpoints (`http://localhost:3000/api/...`).
  - Wire up dynamic DB models for Users, Farmers, Buyers, Products, Orders, Reviews, and Wallets.
  - Implement full filtering, sorting, and pagination logic on the backend for heavy queries.

### Phase 5 & 6: Real API & Authentication Integration
- Implement robust JWT authentication flows with refresh tokens.
- Secure protected routes on the React frontend.
- Standardize Error Messages (e.g., proper 404s, 500s, 401s, 403s) and display user-friendly Toast notifications.

### Phase 7 & 8: Wallet Connect & Arbitrum Smart Contracts
- **MetaMask/Viem integration:** Enable actual wallet connections instead of relying on `localStorage` "mock" addresses.
- Implement the actual transaction signing for the Escrow system (Payment Locks & Payment Releases).
- Reflect actual Arbitrum Sepolia hashes on the frontend Explorer links instead of random `rand::rng()` mocks.

### Phase 9, 10, & 11: UI Polish, Routing, and Performance
- Run a deep audit on broken Links, 404 redirects, and dynamic routes.
- Replace placeholder UI cards with polished, responsive tailwind components.
- Implement proper Skeleton Loaders instead of basic loading text.
- Configure Code Splitting / Lazy Loading for dashboard routes to improve Vite bundle sizes.

### Phase 12, 13, & 14: Security, Testing, & Final QA
- Sanitize inputs across React Hook Forms.
- Thoroughly navigate the app via the simulated browser QA to ensure zero 404s, infinite loaders, or broken images exist.

